        "created_at": "2023-06-25T04:59:18.495Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Ol’ Gloomy is trying to summon himself in the Enclave, and our intrepid heroes need to throw whatever’s on top (or bottom) of their decks at him to thwart his scheme!</p>\n<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/original/2X/3/39673d8f0cc36f2cd7b96541a79970ea7c44b4e8.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/39673d8f0cc36f2cd7b96541a79970ea7c44b4e8\" title=\"20230624233252_1\"><img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/3/39673d8f0cc36f2cd7b96541a79970ea7c44b4e8_2_690x387.jpeg\" alt=\"20230624233252_1\" data-base62-sha1=\"8bOpgobFvKtHbWywtYjN0vNimLe\" width=\"690\" height=\"387\" srcset=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/3/39673d8f0cc36f2cd7b96541a79970ea7c44b4e8_2_690x387.jpeg, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/3/39673d8f0cc36f2cd7b96541a79970ea7c44b4e8_2_1035x580.jpeg 1.5x, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/original/2X/3/39673d8f0cc36f2cd7b96541a79970ea7c44b4e8.jpeg 2x\" data-small-upload=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/3/39673d8f0cc36f2cd7b96541a79970ea7c44b4e8_2_10x10.png\"><div class=\"meta\">\n<svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">20230624233252_1</span><span class=\"informations\">1366×768 330 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg>\n</div></a></div></p>\n<p>I’m shocked that I got this mint. Gloomy played a Cursed Acolyte on the turn he flipped, which killed Parse immediately and brought everyone else low enough they didn’t survive the next villain turn… except for Setback. Thanks to 2 Silver Linings for survival and 2 High Risk Behaviors for damage, he just barely took down the rotting god on his own, for the most Setback-esque victory I’ve ever experienced.</p>",
