        "id": 252956,
        "name": "QuirkyDM",
        "username": "QuirkyDM",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/quirkydm/{size}/2033_2.png",
        "created_at": "2023-06-26T20:36:27.642Z",
        "cooked": "<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/original/2X/4/43837255732b96a65c219760657de5b7c837cc36.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/43837255732b96a65c219760657de5b7c837cc36\" title=\"image\"><img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/4/43837255732b96a65c219760657de5b7c837cc36_2_231x500.jpeg\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"9DfC2FiDaiitqiP80CGX6osWTmm\" width=\"231\" height=\"500\" srcset=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/4/43837255732b96a65c219760657de5b7c837cc36_2_231x500.jpeg, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/4/43837255732b96a65c219760657de5b7c837cc36_2_346x750.jpeg 1.5x, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/4/43837255732b96a65c219760657de5b7c837cc36_2_462x1000.jpeg 2x\" data-small-upload=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/4/43837255732b96a65c219760657de5b7c837cc36_2_10x10.png\"><div class=\"meta\">\n<svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">image</span><span class=\"informations\">828×1792 138 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg>\n</div></a></div></p>\n<p>I seriously considered just playing Setback’s deck all game to see what would happen, but went for the “safer” route instead. Didn’t really worry about much at the start and built Omnitron up to full power - just as he got overloaded with damage and lost all his components while Gloomweaver was still on the first side. After that, I quit “playing around” and told Knyfe to go finish the job while Parse kept the villain deck mostly impotent all game.</p>",
